    "content": "<p>Celebrity blogger Perez Hilton — real name Mario Lavandeira — is recovering in a Miami hospital after a mental health crisis unfolded during a live TikTok broadcast from his home on Tuesday evening, August 4, 2026. Viewers watching the stream grew alarmed as the 48-year-old internet personality appeared to be in serious emotional and physical distress, and many immediately contacted emergency services.</p>\n    <p>The Miami-Dade Sheriff's Office confirmed it received multiple 911 calls beginning around 6:51 p.m. local time from concerned viewers reporting that a livestreamer appeared to be harming himself. Deputies and Miami-Dade Fire Rescue personnel responded to his home in the Westchester neighborhood.</p>\n\n    <h2>A Careful, De-escalation-Focused Response</h2>\n    <p>Rather than force entry, responding deputies — trained in crisis intervention — used what the Sheriff's Office described as an approach built on time, distance, and open communication, speaking with Hilton calmly to help de-escalate the situation. The approach worked: he was safely recovered without anyone being hurt and transported by Miami-Dade Fire Rescue to HCA Florida Kendall Hospital, where he was held under Florida's Baker Act for an involuntary psychiatric evaluation.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"bg-slate-50 p-6 border-l-4 border-[#68A108] my-8 rounded-sm\">\n      <h3 class=\"mt-0 font-serif text-slate-900 font-bold text-base mb-3\">What We Know</h3>\n      <ul class=\"space-y-2 mb-0 list-disc pl-5 text-sm text-slate-700\">\n        <li><strong>Timeline:</strong> First 911 calls came in around 6:51 p.m. on August 4; Hilton was safely recovered and hospitalized the same night.</li>\n        <li><strong>Response:</strong> Miami-Dade deputies used crisis-intervention, de-escalation tactics rather than forced entry.</li>\n        <li><strong>Hospitalization:</strong> Transported to HCA Florida Kendall Hospital and held under Florida's Baker Act for psychiatric evaluation.</li>\n        <li><strong>TikTok's response:</strong> The platform says its automated systems flagged the stream, but a moderator error delayed removal by about 15 minutes; the account has since been permanently banned.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n\n    <h2>Family and Management Respond</h2>\n    <p>Hilton's family said in a statement on Wednesday, August 5, that he is able to communicate, which they said had given them hope, and thanked the viewers and first responders who acted quickly. They asked for privacy while he focuses on recovery.</p>\n    <p>Dante Rusciolelli, co-CEO of Golden Artists Entertainment, which represents Hilton, said the agency spent hours trying to reach him as the stream circulated online, and that its focus now is on his health, his recovery, and his family's privacy.</p>\n    <p>TikTok said its automated moderation systems flagged the broadcast shortly after it began, but that a moderator error delayed the stream's removal by roughly fifteen minutes. The company said it alerted law enforcement and permanently banned Hilton's account for violating its rules on self-harm content.</p>\n\n    <h2>A Difficult Year Before the Crisis</h2>\n    <p>The livestream capped a year in which Hilton had already disclosed serious health struggles. In March 2026, he revealed he had spent 21 days hospitalized after a perforated stomach ulcer led to sepsis. Weeks later, in April, he returned to the hospital for emergency surgery after doctors found a large blood clot — a deep vein thrombosis — in his leg, requiring a thrombectomy.</p>\n    <p>Following those hospitalizations, Hilton spoke publicly about turning to faith during his recovery. Reporting has also pointed to mounting financial pressure in the same period, as medical bills grew and traffic to his long-running celebrity news site declined alongside the broader shift toward short-form video — pressure that friends say compounded an already difficult year.</p>\n\n    <h2>A Long, Complicated Career</h2>\n    <p>Hilton, born Mario Lavandeira Jr., built his fame in the mid-2000s with an aggressively tabloid-style celebrity gossip blog that made him one of the most recognizable — and most criticized — figures on the early internet. In the years since, he has spoken publicly about regretting some of his earlier commentary and shifted his focus toward pop culture, parenting, and daily livestreams with fans.</p>\n    <p>As of Wednesday evening, Hilton remained hospitalized and in stable condition. His family says mental health professionals are supporting him through his recovery, and no discharge date has been announced.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"bg-slate-50 p-6 border-l-4 border-[#68A108] my-8 rounded-sm\">\n      <h3 class=\"mt-0 font-serif text-slate-900 font-bold text-base mb-3\">If You Need Support</h3>\n      <p class=\"text-sm text-slate-700 mb-0\">If you or someone you know is struggling with thoughts of self-harm, free and confidential help is available 24/7. In the US and Canada, call or text <strong>988</strong>, or text <strong>HOME</strong> to <strong>741741</strong> to reach the Crisis Text Line. In the UK, call <strong>116 123</strong>. Internationally, visit <a href=\"https://findahelpline.com\" class=\"underline\">Find A Helpline</a> for local services.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <p>Reporting based on coverage from The Washington Post, NBC News, CBS News, CNN, ABC News, The Hollywood Reporter, and Forbes.</p>"
